    "created_at": "2015-09-04T08:26:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-04T08:26:39Z",
    "body": "I'm not a \"`<canvas>` regular\", but I'm not so sure algorithm-agnostic names like \"fast\" or \"quality\" are actually the best we can do here. If all implementation support both nearest neighbor, linear and bilinear, for example, it would make sense to expose those explicitly. Of course that does not preclude having keywords that map to some of the more specific ones in a user agent-defined way.\n\nJustin Novosad (unknown GitHub handle) and @ds-hwang do a lot of `<canvas>` work in Blink.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
