    "created_at": "2015-09-10T22:51:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-10T22:51:42Z",
    "body": "I think we should follow the (platform) graphics APIs here (e.g. CoreGraphics and Skia) and stick to generic quality levels over algorithm names. Sure, some authors might not get the quality they hoped for, but given that before now they were stuck at low quality, it's probably ok.\n\nTrue professionals are likely to want complete control over the resampling, with knowledge of the types of input images, and whether they are scaling up or down, etc. I don't think anything we do here will completely satisfy them.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
